    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, I'll be a little careful about it. One of the reasons that we have a small group working together, it's some leaders of Main Street and then some leaders of the Freedom Caucus on the Republican side. But one of the reasons that the conversations have been productive in the last 36 hours is because there's a small group of us that we all trust to keep our mouths shut. in trying to figure out how we can negotiate something that we can bring to the floor that can get 218 Republican votes. But I mean, yeah, I mean, we need to get our different, we have a good NDAA, which has passed, which has passed both chambers and needs to go to conference. We need to get defense, Department of Defense approached off the floor. We have to. And part of that, and I don't think anybody, I mean, I think everybody recognizes we're going to need some form of a CR. in order to keep government open. So there's a small group of us trying to figure out what that would look like that can get the Republican votes to pass it over to the Senate and get and start in the negotiation. And I'm more optimistic this morning than I was yesterday morning. And I've learned a long time ago in this town that sometimes that's enough. And we'll keep meeting and we'll keep trying to figure out if we can get there.",
