    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47112.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "So Kelly, two weeks ago, Kevin McCarthy said we're going to have a vote on the floor. Now there's not going to be on the vote on the floor in terms of starting the inquiry. One of the rationales for not needing a vote is because Nancy Pelosi did it in 2019. She started the inquiry without a vote on the floor. So, aren't you basically just doing the same? I mean, the Republican caucus does not like Nancy Pelosi. They didn't like her as a leader, but then justifying your actions based on what she did in 2019 doesn't seem to make a lot of sense to me. So, the actual question is, what changed over the last 10 days or two weeks where McCarthy went from absolutely we're going to have a vote to we don't need to have a vote other than politics?",
