    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47112.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "I don't know. I mean, I'm not a part of that. But I mean, I said that. And I mean, by the way, I was critical of that then. But it goes back to this. I mean, it goes back to the same thing. When you do something, you create a precedent that will be used against you or used in the same manner moving forward. And that is true. I think I said this before. There is somebody at Redmi Speaker McCarthy's quote, and I said, sure, you can call that hypocrisy, or you can say imitation is the sincerest form of flattery. But the reality is, is once you've done it once, it's going to be the new mode of doing things here. And whether that's unfortunate or not, by the way, I think eventually we'll need a vote. And I think Speaker Pelosi recognized that as well, but you can designate this to the committees and put those purposes. The in the weeds portion of this is all congressional investigations need a legislative purpose. And impeachment inquiry is its own legislative purpose. So our guiding light should be for us if we are being like National Archives emails, DOJ now all of a sudden saying we can't talk to you because we have an active investigation. And by active, I mean, for four and a half years, you put a file on top of that file. And then whenever that file got to the top, you put another file on top of that file and only became really active and sometime in the last three months. So if it gives us our best position to get the information that we're entitled to and the American people are entitled to see in court, I'm all for it. I'm not interested in doing this simply to make our base feel better. I think that's a bad idea. But I also think that there is a lot of questions and a lot of information that we can glean some things from through shell corporations and different statements and changing statements and all of those different things. And if this gives us our best position in court to get the documents we want, then I'm all for it.",
