    "turn_text": "you allow me to get to the point, I was going to make that point, Chad. The problem I have is that a lot of the Republicans who are wanting to impeach Joe Biden and investigate Hunter Biden into all of this stuff are simultaneously castigating the Department of Justice for investigating Donald Trump, or they're trying to, we have members of Republican members of Congress who are trying to fiddle around in the state of Georgia's prosecution of Donald Trump. That's something that really bothers me. When I look at both sides, we have liberals who are very much in favor of going after Donald Trump who want to put the breaks on investigating Joe Biden's relationship with Hunter Biden's business practices. But then on the other hand, you have people who want to investigate Hunter Biden and Joe Biden, but they don't want to investigate Donald Trump or Rudy Giuliani or a lot of these other things. That seems like hypocrisy on both sides. And I wish, I mean, every time I hear one side, you know, make the case, I say, okay, great. Now apply it to the other side. Why can't we have equal standards here?",
