    "turn_text": "and it's not. But I would be clear. If the president's son is in recovery and not using drugs and doing all of those things, I have no interest in any of that stuff, none. I don't care. I think you both know me well enough to know that is absolutely something I don't think the United States Congress should be setting his time on. Now, if I have $20 million that is moving through companies, shell companies, then I have no idea what they do. And by the way, nobody else seems to be able to answer that question either. And the answer can't just be, oh, it's a legitimate business purpose. Okay, what's the legitimate business purpose? And I have a White House that I will be as sympathetic to as possible that has significantly changed their version of their interaction with these events four different times. And a DOJ that direct or a White House transition team that directly interfered with an FBI investigation in order to get an interview with Hunter Biden. I think you all know and there are a lot of things that a presidential transition team does. they don't have any investigative function. It is a purely political enterprise. So these are questions that I think are more than willing to ask. I think I applaud particularly Chairman Comer for doing this in a manner in which we're actually putting together, you know, linear evidence with what we have. And I think that is an appropriate place to be and particularly considering when you do have people that think people People are treated very differently depending on what side of the aisle you're on.",
