  {
    "episode_id": 47112,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47112.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 50,
    "turn_text": "Well, I would absolutely, I don't think you should worry about it, Chad. I think that's the reality of it. I said that during the last impeachment, to say that you have 100 impartial jurors in the United States Senate, Congress is really bad at pretending it's something it's not. It's a partisan body. That's why the DOJ and the criminal justice system has to be fair and impartial. There's nothing that happens in this town that is fair and impartial. And we should be honest about that, and we should talk about it. But if I am defending a client and my jury pool and it's political and my jury pool is 100 US senators, I can strike all 100 of them on both sides of the aisle for cause. So let's not pretend that that it is what it is. And in that, I mean, we should remember, and everybody watching this should know this, the US said it is not going to convict Joe Biden of",
