    "turn_text": "You know, speaking about that, I don't know a lot of people know this. When I worked as a private investigator, we did criminal defense work. My father was a retired police officer, did a lot of criminal. We would get appointed in federal cases to represent, you know, for instance, you know, here in North Dakota, a lot of the federal cases happen on the reservation. So we would be appointed to represent the defendant who did not have a lot of means And we would be up against a case built by maybe 25 FBI agents who touch the case, hundreds and hundreds of man hours put into this case. The federal government would appoint us and give us a $1,500 budget to rebut that investigation.",
