    "turn_text": "But that's what the one part I will say on the federal prosecution of Donald Trump that really, really frustrates me is Jack Smith in a filing to the court because they asked for continues. We can talk about all of that. But essentially the Trump defense team said if we read one page of discovery a minute, a one page a minute. This we wouldn't get through all the discovery you provided us in time to go to trial a year after you're asking for the trial date or something along that lines. And the response from the Special Counsel's Office was essentially, well, almost exactly, the defense is based on the faulty premise that they have to read all the discovery to provide an adequate defense. That is not a faulty premise. By the way, this happens in federal court with prosecutors and defense attorneys all the time. But you've been looking at somebody for however period in time. But the reality is, I would, my immediate brief and response would have been, okay, you tell me which pages I don't have to look at and those will be the first ones",
