  {
    "episode_id": 47112,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47112.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 68,
    "turn_text": "So I'm gonna shift us back to government shutdown a little bit. I mean, we're on speaking of being on a hamster wheels, right? I mean, I feel like with the impeachment and maybe January 6th and not trusting elections, I feel like we're starting a hamster wheel there where both parties are going to go back and forth. But the government shutdown thing, I mean, I think the last time we were looking at a government shutdown, I think we had you on and you were, or maybe I talked to you at the airport, but you were feeling confident that it would get done and then it got done. You seemed a little less confident at the beginning of this podcast. Should I as somebody who cares about the Minot Air Force folks getting paid and all those? Should we be reading into that? Is this getting harder and harder the closer we get to elections to actually keep government open?",
