    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/7/47112.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 84,
    "turn_text": "I just finished up our interview with Kelly Armstrong, and I'll tell you, Chad, I'm glad I don't have to do negotiations on a continuing resolution or something like that. Although it's amazing how far we've moved the goal post, because a continuing resolution in and of itself is a failure. Right. If we're having to pass a continuing resolution, that means we couldn't pass budgets. We live in a country where we can't budget even. And now it's so dysfunctional. It's like, well, it's a good thing if we pass it. I mean, it used to be passed having to being forced to pass a continuing resolution as opposed to just doing the normal budget. was considered like a bad thing, but now it's like a choice between if we do a continuing resolution, instead of shutting the entire government down, then oh, well, we've really accomplished something. And it's not me besmirching. I mean, Kelly's working in a, I mean, the",
