    "turn_text": "worry about that environment. We tried to get to it and, but I worry about, we've talked a lot about this in the past, that, you know, Congress is of one party, so they're gonna impeach the president of the other party, pretty soon it doesn't mean anything. And we're, do we miss out on real problems because, and I don't know what's gonna come out of this inquiry, but if we're constantly in an impeachment inquiry, no matter who the president is, it's a problem. We've talked about January 6th setting up a precedent of if one party loses the election to not believe the outcomes. I would hope Democrats would handle it better, but I'm not so sure that's the case if Donald Trump were to get elected in 2024.",
