    "turn_text": "Yeah, that's what it is. And because I also wanted one thing that I've talked about, especially with the legislature, is how much of a luxury some of the quote unquote most conservative lawmakers have, they have this luxury where they can cut like you're a Jeff Magrimmer or somebody like that. And you can sit back and just vote against everything. And you get these perfect scores on these scorecards. Look at how conservative I am. right but that's that's that's the easy button that's not governing that's not running as hard right social governing is like well we have to fund the schools and in order to fund the schools uh i'm gonna have to give up some things that i don't like in order for us to pass it like we are constitutionally obligated to fund the schools constitution says we got to have schools we got to fund them So, you know, we have to do it in order to get there, to get a number of votes to do it. And by the way, also because the governor's part of the process, to get the governor to sign off on it, to sign in the law, you have to compromise. And you're not gonna get everything you want. And so, what they're scoring on is completely alien to the process of governing. Because the process of governing is like, well, I gotta negotiate with people, whether, I mean, sometimes they're Democrats that disagree with you. Sometimes they're other Republicans. who disagree with you for reasons of ideology or reasons that there may be",
